"1\n00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,229\nThe Learning Brain. Series 3: Generative AI\n\n2\n00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:07,333\nEpisode 2\n\n3\n00:00:07,413 --> 00:00:08,986\nOffloading\n\n4\n00:00:11,786 --> 00:00:15,072\nStudents studied a list of words in one computer file,\n\n5\n00:00:15,309 --> 00:00:16,899\nthen a second list in another.\n\n6\n00:00:17,427 --> 00:00:20,310\nWhen they saved the first file before moving on,\n\n7\n00:00:20,507 --> 00:00:22,596\nthey remembered more of the second list.\n\n8\n00:00:23,077 --> 00:00:26,172\nOffloading the first list freed room for the next.\n\n9\n00:00:26,342 --> 00:00:29,270\nPsychologists call this cognitive offloading: using the world,\n\n10\n00:00:29,668 --> 00:00:31,360\na note, a device,\n\n11\n00:00:31,555 --> 00:00:32,701\nor now an AI,\n\n12\n00:00:32,721 --> 00:00:36,060\nto lower the demand on your own head.\n\n13\n00:00:36,511 --> 00:00:38,008\nIt is as old as writing,\n\n14\n00:00:38,028 --> 00:00:39,161\nand often smart.\n\n15\n00:00:39,331 --> 00:00:41,102\nBut offloading has a cost.\n\n16\n00:00:41,515 --> 00:00:43,403\nIn a pattern copying task,\n\n17\n00:00:43,634 --> 00:00:46,793\npeople who offloaded more performed better in the moment,\n\n18\n00:00:47,040 --> 00:00:48,886\nand remembered less afterwards.\n\n19\n00:00:49,314 --> 00:00:53,667\nThat held across three experiments of a hundred and seventy two people each.\n\n20\n00:00:53,837 --> 00:00:55,504\nThe cost was not fixed.\n\n21\n00:00:55,840 --> 00:00:58,237\nWhen people knew a memory test was coming,\n\n22\n00:00:58,414 --> 00:01:01,339\nthey could almost entirely make up for offloading.\n\n23\n00:01:01,759 --> 00:01:04,356\nIntending to learn changed what stayed.\n\n24\n00:01:04,526 --> 00:01:10,088\nThe saving benefit also vanished when people were told the saved file might not be there.\n\n25\n00:01:10,652 --> 00:01:14,197\nOffloading only frees the mind when the store is trusted.\n\n26\n00:01:14,367 --> 00:01:18,754\nOne famous claim, that hard questions make us think of searching the internet,\n\n27\n00:01:18,987 --> 00:01:20,281\nfailed to replicate.\n\n28\n00:01:20,803 --> 00:01:23,316\nThe broad pattern of offloading is solid.\n\n29\n00:01:23,637 --> 00:01:25,645\nSome striking headlines are not.\n\n30\n00:01:25,815 --> 00:01:26,618\nA caution.\n\n31\n00:01:26,961 --> 00:01:29,856\nThese are lab tasks with lists and patterns.\n\n32\n00:01:30,160 --> 00:01:33,189\nGenerative AI can offload more than memory.\n\n33\n00:01:33,445 --> 00:01:35,782\nIt can offload the reasoning itself.\n\n34\n00:01:35,952 --> 00:01:36,726\nFor teaching.\n\n35\n00:01:37,108 --> 00:01:39,946\nDecide what students must hold in their own heads,\n\n36\n00:01:39,966 --> 00:01:40,772\nand say so.\n\n37\n00:01:41,165 --> 00:01:42,594\nLet them offload the rest,\n\n38\n00:01:42,614 --> 00:01:44,758\nand tell them when a test is coming,\n\n39\n00:01:44,778 --> 00:01:46,449\nso they learn on purpose.\n\n40\n00:01:46,836 --> 00:01:48,540\nAnd when AI does a step,\n\n41\n00:01:48,805 --> 00:01:51,112\nhave them restate it in their own words.\n\n42\n00:01:51,282 --> 00:01:53,144\nOffloading is not the problem.\n\n43\n00:01:53,474 --> 00:01:55,840\nOffloading what you were meant to learn is.\n\n"
